  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115942",
      "title": "Building a First Custom Pipe",
      "lectureOrder": 167,
      "videoOrder": 159,
      "sourceHash": "7c7e2ac80bd9eddcc7e066ad46fc2709a87b83ebf40906c269914ab674fd69ca",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.57,
          "end": 2.61,
          "en": "So let's build a custom pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.61,
          "end": 3.87,
          "en": "And I wanna build a pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 3.87,
          "end": 7.05,
          "en": "that, again, formats these temperature values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.05,
          "end": 10.23,
          "en": "but also these temperature values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.23,
          "end": 14.01,
          "en": "To be precise, I wanna build a custom pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.01,
          "end": 18.06,
          "en": "that can be used for outputting these values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.06,
          "end": 19.86,
          "en": "as temperature values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.86,
          "end": 24.86,
          "en": "by adding the appropriate symbol in degrees Celsius",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.21,
          "end": 26.79,
          "en": "or degrees Fahrenheit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.79,
          "end": 30.03,
          "en": "And in addition, the pipe should also be able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.03,
          "end": 35.03,
          "en": "to convert values from Celsius to Fahrenheit and vice versa.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.51,
          "end": 38.7,
          "en": "So it will do two things,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.7,
          "end": 41.67,
          "en": "convert the values that are being output,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.67,
          "end": 44.97,
          "en": "and also add a fitting temperature symbol",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.97,
          "end": 47.82,
          "en": "for Celsius or Fahrenheit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.82,
          "end": 51.3,
          "en": "And therefore, to add a new pipe, I'll add a new file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.3,
          "end": 53.07,
          "en": "We could also use the CLI,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.07,
          "end": 57.18,
          "en": "but again, I'll do that manually here for this first pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.18,
          "end": 61.353,
          "en": "And I'll add a temperature pipe, TS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.21,
          "end": 65.91,
          "en": "As always, we have a name that describes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.91,
          "end": 67.74,
          "en": "what this thing is about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.74,
          "end": 70.17,
          "en": "Then we describe what kind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.17,
          "end": 73.28999999999999,
          "en": "of Angular feature we're using or building",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.28999999999999,
          "end": 76.863,
          "en": "and then .ts, since we're using TypeScript, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.3,
          "end": 83.01,
          "en": "Well, and then in there, a pipe is also just a class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83.01,
          "end": 86.03999999999999,
          "en": "just like Components or Directives.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.03999999999999,
          "end": 87.9,
          "en": "It's a class which I want to export",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.9,
          "end": 91.35,
          "en": "to make it available outside of this file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.35,
          "end": 93.887,
          "en": "And then I'll name it TemperaturePipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 95.43,
          "end": 98.72999999999999,
          "en": "Now, this class should then, as a next step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.72999999999999,
          "end": 102.03,
          "en": "be decorated with the Pipe decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.03,
          "end": 104.22,
          "en": "Just as we use component for Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.22,
          "end": 107.55,
          "en": "and directive for Directives, we use the Pipe decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.55,
          "end": 110.343,
          "en": "to turn a class into a pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 111.75,
          "end": 114.50999999999999,
          "en": "And just as all these other decorators,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114.50999999999999,
          "end": 118.25999999999999,
          "en": "this Pipe decorator takes a configuration object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.25999999999999,
          "end": 121.62,
          "en": "where we can, for example, give this pipe a name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.62,
          "end": 124.77,
          "en": "And indeed, we must give this pipe a name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.77,
          "end": 126.54,
          "en": "This is not optional.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 126.54,
          "end": 127.56,
          "en": "We need a name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.56,
          "end": 131.22,
          "en": "because it's that name by which we'll use that pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.22,
          "end": 132.843,
          "en": "in a template thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.83,
          "end": 135.75,
          "en": "And here I'll use temp as a name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 135.75,
          "end": 137.25,
          "en": "but of course it is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 138.32999999999998,
          "end": 141.9,
          "en": "I'll then also set this to be a standalone pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 141.9,
          "end": 145.29,
          "en": "The alternative would be to not make it standalone",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 145.29,
          "end": 148.82999999999998,
          "en": "and instead use NG modules just as we did it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 148.82999999999998,
          "end": 151.77,
          "en": "with Components earlier in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 151.77,
          "end": 155.16,
          "en": "But here I'll use standalone as I've always done it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 155.16,
          "end": 157.86,
          "en": "for all the Components and all the Directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 157.86,
          "end": 160.56,
          "en": "in the previous sections.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 160.56,
          "end": 163.65,
          "en": "So that's then a basic pipe which we could use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 163.65,
          "end": 166.17000000000002,
          "en": "But this pipe wouldn't do anything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 166.17000000000002,
          "end": 167.8,
          "en": "and wouldn't actually work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 168.75,
          "end": 170.94,
          "en": "because all those pipe classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 170.94,
          "end": 175.683,
          "en": "need one very specific method, transform method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 178.53,
          "end": 181.41,
          "en": "And it's this transform method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181.41,
          "end": 183.69,
          "en": "that will be executed automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 183.69,
          "end": 188.49,
          "en": "by Angular when you use this pipe we're building here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 188.49,
          "end": 193.49,
          "en": "in a template, and the value after which you use that pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 194.01,
          "end": 198.24,
          "en": "will be passed as an argument to this transform method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 198.24,
          "end": 200.7,
          "en": "But we'll see this in action soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 200.7,
          "end": 202.62,
          "en": "And since this is required,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 202.62,
          "end": 206.97,
          "en": "and to make sure that you have the right method signature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 206.97,
          "end": 209.1,
          "en": "that you accept the right arguments,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 209.1,
          "end": 211.89,
          "en": "and you have no typo in that method name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 211.89,
          "end": 213.6,
          "en": "since all that matters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 213.6,
          "end": 218.13,
          "en": "Angular gives us an interface which we can implement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 218.13,
          "end": 220.2,
          "en": "into this pipe class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 220.2,
          "end": 223.02,
          "en": "The PipeTransform interface,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 223.02,
          "end": 225.663,
          "en": "which is imported from @Angular/core,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 227.67000000000002,
          "end": 230.01,
          "en": "which simply forces me",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 230.01,
          "end": 234.3,
          "en": "to add a transform method written like that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 234.3,
          "end": 237.42000000000002,
          "en": "which accepts a value as a first argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 237.42000000000002,
          "end": 241.59,
          "en": "and then any number of additional arguments thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 241.59,
          "end": 243.21,
          "en": "And we'll tweak the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 243.21,
          "end": 245.85,
          "en": "and the additional arguments in just a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 245.85,
          "end": 250.29,
          "en": "But this is a method that must exist in such a pipe class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 250.29,
          "end": 252.093,
          "en": "for that pipe to work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 253.98,
          "end": 257.49,
          "en": "And this transform method then also must return something.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 257.49,
          "end": 260.67,
          "en": "It must return the transformed value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 260.67,
          "end": 263.97,
          "en": "which will then, in the end, be output on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 263.97,
          "end": 268.08,
          "en": "So in its simplest form, we can simply return the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 268.08,
          "end": 270.243,
          "en": "as we get it without changing it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 271.23,
          "end": 273.72,
          "en": "Or to see that something has changed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 273.72,
          "end": 277.623,
          "en": "we could add dash transformed thereafter, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 278.61,
          "end": 280.32,
          "en": "So I am taking any value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 280.32,
          "end": 282.48,
          "en": "and then I'm converting it to a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 282.48,
          "end": 285.183,
          "en": "that has dash transformed at the end of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 286.86,
          "end": 287.90999999999997,
          "en": "Well, and with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 287.90999999999997,
          "end": 291.27,
          "en": "we would have a first basic custom pipe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 291.27,
          "end": 293.58,
          "en": "which doesn't do anything useful yet though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 293.58,
          "end": 296.31,
          "en": "but we'll take care of that soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 296.31,
          "end": 297.99,
          "en": "For the moment, to use this pipe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 297.99,
          "end": 299.7,
          "en": "we have to go to a template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 299.7,
          "end": 301.68,
          "en": "in this case, to the app component template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 301.68,
          "end": 303.063,
          "en": "since this is the only one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 304.59,
          "end": 306.15,
          "en": "And then here, we can use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 306.15,
          "end": 309.483,
          "en": "anywhere where we're outputting dynamic content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 310.47,
          "end": 314.82,
          "en": "So for example, here, instead of using the number pipe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 314.82,
          "end": 319.82,
          "en": "instead of doing that, we could use the temp pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 320.04,
          "end": 321.273,
          "en": "we just created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 322.62,
          "end": 325.32,
          "en": "But as always, Angular wouldn't know it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 325.32,
          "end": 327.03,
          "en": "So to unlock it, we have to go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 327.03,
          "end": 329.28,
          "en": "to the app component TypeScript file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 329.28,
          "end": 332.76,
          "en": "and add our temperature pipe here to the imports",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 332.76,
          "end": 335.163,
          "en": "and also add this import at the top.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 337.74,
          "end": 340.65,
          "en": "And with that, the temp pipe is unlocked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 340.65,
          "end": 343.203,
          "en": "And if you now save everything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 344.4,
          "end": 349.11,
          "en": "you will see dash transformed here for this first value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 349.11,
          "end": 352.40999999999997,
          "en": "And that proves that our pipe is working.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 352.40999999999997,
          "end": 355.713,
          "en": "Now it's time to make it actually useful.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
